.TH HD-AGENT 8 "November 2026" "hd-agent" "HyprDebian"
.SH NAME
hd-agent \- send the state of the system to the hyprdebian dashboard and run its jobs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hd-agent
.RB [ \-\-print ]
.br
.B hd-agent run
.I sequence
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hd-agent
collects the state of the system and POSTs it as a JSON report to the
hyprdebian dashboard, see
.BR hd-dashboard (7).
The system only makes outgoing connections.
The reply has the jobs for the system, made by
.BR hd-manager (1),
which
.B hd-agent
accepts and runs at their time, see
.BR JOBS .
.PP
.B hd-agent.timer
runs it through
.B hd-agent.service
2 minutes after the boot and then every 15 minutes, with up to a minute of
random delay.
The package enables the timer on its first installation; after that, it stays
as the admin left it.
When the dashboard cannot be reached or refuses the report, the service fails
and the error is in its journal:
.PP
.RS
journalctl \-u hd-agent.service
.RE
.PP
Run it as root: the token is only readable by root.
.PP
The package replaces
.BR hd-report :
installing it removes
.BR hd-report ,
and takes over its token from
.IR /etc/hyprdebian/hd-report/token ,
its settings, the key
.BR hd-report ,
which becomes the key
.BR hd-agent ,
and the enabled state of
.BR hd-report.timer .
The dashboard keeps accepting the reports of the system.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ,\  \-\-help
Show a short help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-print
Only print the report, without sending it.
That also works as a normal user, without the parts only root can read, the
jobs among them.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI run\  sequence
Run the stored job with that sequence number; its timer does that, see
.BR JOBS .
.SH SETTINGS
The settings are the key
.B hd-agent
of
.IR /etc/hyprdebian/config.json ,
see
.BR hd-config (7).
A setting that is missing has its default value, from
.IR /usr/share/hd-agent/defaults.json .
.TP
.B url
The URL of the dashboard, with
.B http://
or
.BR https:// ;
the report goes to
.IR <url>/report .
The default is
.BR http://dash.rsq\-online.ddns.net/ .
.TP
.B manager_keys
The public keys of the managers, as
.B hd-manager key
prints them: Ed25519 keys, one per string.
A job must be signed by one of them.
The default is
.BR [] :
without keys the agent sends its reports, but accepts no jobs.
.B hd-agent run
reads them again, so a job whose key is taken off the list no longer runs.
.PP
For example:
.PP
.RS
sudo hd-config-update hd-agent '{"url": "http://dash.example/", "manager_keys": ["ssh-ed25519 AAAA... hd-manager@beast"]}'
.RE
.SH TOKEN
The token of the system is in
.IR /etc/hyprdebian/hd-agent/token ,
mode 0600.
The installation generates it when there is none, and never replaces it:
the dashboard accepts the first token it sees for a host name, and only that
token afterwards.
A purge of the package keeps it too.
When the token is lost, as on a reinstalled system, forget the host on the
dashboard with
.BR "hd-dashboard forget" ,
and the next report registers the new token.
.SH THE REPORT
The host name, the FQDN, the version of HyprDebian from
.IR /etc/hyprdebian/version.json ,
the suite of the HyprDebian packages, the Debian
version, the running and the newest installed kernel, the boot time, the
state of Secure Boot as
.BR hd-secboot (8)
finds it, the load, the CPUs, the memory, the ZFS pools with their last
completed scrub, the mdadm arrays, the
state of systemd and the failed units, the upgradable packages from the
package lists apt has now, the last upgrade, a pending
reboot as
.BR hd-reboot-check (1)
finds it, the newest
.B hd-up
snapshot of
.IR rpool/hyprdebian ,
and the enabled timers in
.I /etc/systemd/system
and the
.B hd-*
timers of the packages, with the result of their last run, and the state of
each part that
.BR hd-harden (8)
hardens, as
.B hd-harden \-\-json
prints it.
And the stored jobs: those that have not ended as
.BR scheduled ,
also a running one, and the ended ones with their result, start and end
time.
This is report format 2.
.SH JOBS
A job is one command for one system, to run once, not before
.B not_before
and not after
.BR expires ,
signed by a manager.
.B hd-agent
accepts a job of the reply when its signature verifies against one of
.BR manager_keys ,
its host is the host name of this system, and its sequence number is higher
than that of the last job it accepted.
It ignores any other job; one it accepted before silently, the others with a
line in the journal.
.PP
An accepted job is stored in
.IR /var/lib/hd-agent/jobs/<sequence>.json ,
as
.BR scheduled .
A newer job with the same command cancels a job that is still scheduled; a
running job is never cancelled.
.PP
The timer
.BI hd-agent-job- sequence .timer\fR,
a transient unit of
.BR systemd-run (1),
starts the service
.BI hd-agent-job- sequence .service
at
.BR not_before ,
which runs
.BI "hd-agent run " sequence\fR.
A reboot loses the transient timers, so every run of
.B hd-agent
makes them again, before it sends the report.
A job whose
.B not_before
passed, as while the system was off, runs at once; one whose expiry passed is
.BR expired ;
one that was running when the system went down
.BR failed .
.PP
.B hd-agent run
checks the signature and the expiry again, runs the command and stores the
result:
.B ok
when it ended with 0,
.B failed
otherwise, and also when the signature no longer verifies.
The command
.B upgrade
runs
.BR "hd-up \-\-unattended" ,
which never reboots.
The output is in the journal:
.PP
.RS
journalctl \-u hd-agent-job-<sequence>.service
.RE
.PP
The report has every stored job.
An ended job is removed from the store once it is no longer in
.B open
of a reply, the jobs the dashboard has no end for.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when the report was sent or printed, 1 on an error, 2 on wrong arguments.
.B hd-agent run
exits with 0 when the job ended ok, and 1 when it did not run or did not end
ok.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/hyprdebian/config.json
The settings, in the key
.BR hd-agent .
.TP
.I /usr/share/hd-agent/defaults.json
The default settings.
.TP
.I /etc/hyprdebian/hd-agent/token
The token of the system.
.TP
.I /var/lib/hd-agent/jobs/<sequence>.json
A stored job, with its state.
.TP
.I /var/lib/hd-agent/sequence
The highest sequence number accepted.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/hd-agent.timer
.TQ
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/hd-agent.service
Run hd-agent every 15 minutes.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hd-dashboard (7),
.BR hd-manager (1),
.BR hd-config-update (1),
.BR hd-harden (8),
.BR hd-secboot (8),
.BR hd-up (1)
